// U11 (D-JPK-SCRIPTDEP1=A): a bare script — no `pkg.jet` — declares a
// dependency inline with `use pkg#version;` instead of a manifest. `jet run`
// resolves it (here, from the committed `.jet/inline-deps/textkit/1.4.2/`
// copy — no network, no pkg.jet) and runs. `jet store lock main.jet` would pin
// this in a `main.jet.lock` sidecar; `jet init main.jet` would lift it into
// a generated `pkg.jet` so the project can grow past rung 0.
use textkit#1.4.2

fn run() {
    print(textkit.shout("hello from an inline dependency"))
}
